==Battleground==
*5 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 6~12 seconds<sup>180f~360f</sup>.
*1 [[General GreGory]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Squire Rel]] spawns as the boss.
**30 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
**8 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
**3 [[Project A]]s spawn, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
**1 [[I.M. Phace]] spawns.
**3 [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn, delay 30~40 seconds<sup>900f~1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn, delay 8~12 seconds<sup>240f~360f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage has a very high pushing power from the deadly combination of Rain D., General GreGory, and I.M. Phace.

For the startoff, there are only a few Those Guys and a singular General GreGory. On 1* difficulty, you can try to finish the GreGory off with [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]], or try to have [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] trade with GreGory so that both of them die.

Once the I.M. Phace dies, be careful not to spend all your cash if the Rain Ds are in the Project A's range, as spamming [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance units]] or attackers will just cause them to run in and most likely die.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Extremely helpful on this stage, being able to minimize the pushing power of the enemies even if your units die.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]: Primarily being used to deal with the 3 GreGories. Once the GreGories die, the enemies lose a large amount of pushing power.
*Any generic Long Distance attacker can prove to be of use, such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]] or [[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]] ([[True Form]] only). Housewife Cat and Bubble Cat both deal high damage per hit to ward off the Rain Ds, while Fried Chicken's Curse can disable the Project A's disruptive warp.

